# Firebase sign-in (Google): the script hosts below are needed for it. The sign-in pages under /__/auth/ are proxied from
# Firebase (see _redirects), so the Content-Security-Policy is set only on the app's own pages, never on /__/auth/*.
# No default-src, connect-src or img-src on purpose: the app talks to Firestore, Google sign-in and the book/map services,
# and a list written by hand could silently break one of them. Inline scripts stay blocked by script-src (which also keeps
# the Netlify badge from being injected); object-src, base-uri, form-action and frame-ancestors close the other gaps.
/
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' https://apis.google.com https://www.gstatic.com https://www.google.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
/index.html
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' https://apis.google.com https://www.gstatic.com https://www.google.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()
